The pairs are distinguished by the indices of the mochi used, not just their sizes. However, the problem statement says "Two kagamimochi are distinguished if at least one of the mochi is different, even if the sizes of the mochi are the same." This implies we are counting pairs of indices $(i, j)$ such that $i \neq j$ and $A_i \le A_j / 2$. Wait, let's re-read carefully.
