        # Print the result
        print(result)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```
Using `sys.stdin.read().strip()` handles cases where there might be extra whitespace around the input better than `input()`, although `input()` is usually fine for single line. Given the simplicity, `input()` is perfectly acceptable and standard
