The squared distance of a vertex $(x, y)$ from the origin is $x^2 + y^2$.
We need $\max((i+0.5)^2 + (j+0.5)^2, (i+0.5)^2 + (j-0.5)^2, (i-0.5)^2 + (j+0.5)^2, (i-0.5)^2 + (j-0.5)^2) \le R^2$.
Notice that $(i \pm 0.5)^2 + (j \pm 0.5)^2$ takes values based on the signs.
$(i+0.5)^2 + (j+0.5)^2 = i^2 + i + 0.25 + j^2 + j + 0.25 = i^2 + j^2 + i + j + 0.5$.
